+      - id: R4\n+        text: \"Implement srd082 R7.3: multi-file argument support -- process each file argument in order, printing output for each file separated by blank lines in default mode, and continuing past errors to process all arguments\"\n+\n+    design_decisions:\n+      - id: D1\n+        text: Error messages must match GNU stat format exactly -- read srd082-stat.yaml R7.1 for the required error message template.\n+      - id: D2\n+        text: Exit code is the logical OR of all per-file results -- 1 if any file fails, 0 only if all succeed. This matches GNU coreutils convention.\n+      - id: D3\n+        text: Terse output with --file-system uses a different field set than terse output for files -- read srd082-stat.yaml R6.1 for both formats.\n+\n+    acceptance_criteria:\n+      - id: AC1\n+        text: \"go build -o bin/stat ./cmd/stat/ succeeds\"\n+      - id: AC2\n+        text: \"bin/stat --terse on a regular file prints a single line of space-separated metadata fields\"\n+      - id: AC3\n+        text: \"bin/stat nonexistent_file prints 'stat: cannot stat ...' to stderr and exits 1\"\n+      - id: AC4\n+        text: \"bin/stat file1 nonexistent file2 prints output for file1 and file2, error for nonexistent to stderr, and exits 1\"\n+      - id: AC5\n+        text: \"go vet ./cmd/stat/... reports no errors\"\n+  dependency: 2","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bcba697-70f2-4b61-a9af-34eaf485d661","uuid":"b88999a3-3413-4cf1-b1e6-1e6df66f0fcf","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:57:54.390Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"diff --git a/.cobbler/measure.yaml b/.cobbler/measure.yaml\nindex c988f011..9b8df5bd 100644\n--- a/.cobbler/measure.yaml\n+++ b/.cobbler/measure.yaml\n@@ -17417,3 +17417,181 @@\n       - id: AC6\n         text: \"go vet ./cmd/sync/ reports no issues after modifications\"\n   dependency: 2\n+- index: 0\n+  title: '[stitch] cmd/stat (contract) (srd082)'\n+  description: |\n+    deliverable_type: code\n+\n+    re