d: AC5\n+        text: \"go vet ./cmd/stat/... reports no errors\"\n+  dependency: 1\n+- index: 3\n+  title: '[stitch] Implement cmd/stat terse output and error handling (srd082 R6.1, R7.1, R7.2, R7.3)'\n+  description: |-\n+    deliverable_type: code\n+\n+    required_reading:\n+      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd082-stat.yaml (R6.1, R7.1, R7.2, R7.3 -- terse mode, error reporting, exit codes, multi-file)\n+      - cmd/stat/main.go (implementation from prior tasks)\n+      - CLAUDE.md (project conventions)\n+\n+    files:\n+      - path: cmd/stat/main.go\n+        action: modify\n+        note: Implement terse output mode and error handling\n+\n+    requirements:\n+      - id: R1\n+        text: \"Implement srd082 R6.1: --terse / -t option that prints file information as a single compact line of space-separated fields in the format specified by srd082-stat.yaml (typically: name size blocks mode uid gid device inode links major minor atime mtime ctime birthtime)\"\n+      - id: R2\n+        text: \"Implement srd082 R7.1: error reporting for non-existent or inaccessible files -- print error message to stderr in the format matching GNU stat (e.g., \\\"stat: cannot stat 'FILENAME': No such file or directory\\\") and continue processing remaining arguments\"\n+      - id: R3\n+        text: \"Implement srd082 R7.2: exit code handling -- exit 0 when all files are processed successfully, exit 1 when any file produces an error\"\n+      - id: R4\n+        text: \"Implement srd082 R7.3: multi-file argument support -- process each file argument in order, printing output for each file separated by blank lines in default mode, and continuing past errors to process all arguments\"\n+\n+    design_decisions:\n+      - id: D1\n+        text: Error messages must match GNU stat format exactly -- read srd082-stat.yaml R7.1 for the required error message template.\n+      - id: D2\n+        text: Exit code is the logical OR of all per-file results -- 1 if any file fails, 0 only if all succeed. This matches GNU coreutils convention.\n+      - id: D3\n+        text: Terse output with --file-system uses a different field set than terse output for files -- read srd082-stat.yaml R6.1 for both formats.\n+\n+    acceptance_criteria:\n+      - id: AC1\n+        text: \"go build -o bin/stat ./cmd/stat/ succeeds\"\n+      - id: AC2\n+        text: \"bin/stat --terse on a regular file prints a single line of space-separated metadata fields\"\n+      - id: AC3\n+        text: \"bin/stat nonexistent_file prints 'stat: cannot stat ...' to stderr and exits 1\"\n+      - id: AC4\n+        text: \"bin/stat file1 nonexistent file2 prints output for file1 and file2, error for nonexistent to stderr, and exits 1\"\n+      - id: AC5\n+        text: \"go vet ./cmd/stat/... reports no errors\"\n+  dependency: 2","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
