{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VoTp3FNM3kD9CXn7w9UDer","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd082-stat\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/stat: Display File Status\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD stat that differs from GNU stat in default output format, format\n6\t  string syntax, and flag names. GNU stat supports printf-style format strings for\n7\t  customizable output. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n8\t  (gstat, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, verified by\n9\t  differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Display file status information (size, permissions, timestamps, inode, etc.).\n13\t  - G2: Support printf-style format strings for custom output via --format (-c).\n14\t  - G3: Support filesystem status mode via --file-system (-f).\n15\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gstat via differential testing.\n16\t\n17\trequirements:\n18\t  R1:\n19\t    title: Default file status\n20\t    items:\n21\t      - R1.1:\n22\t          text: Must display file status for each named file argument using the default multi-line format matching GNU stat output (File, Size, Blocks, IO Block, file type, Device, Inode, Links, Access mode, Uid, Gid, Access time, Modify time, Change time, Birth time).\n23\t\n24\t  R2:\n25\t    title: File listing options\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R2.1:\n28\t          text: Must process multiple file arguments in order, printing status for each.\n29\t      - R2.2:\n30\t          text: \"-L or --dereference must follow symlinks and report the target file's status instead of the link itself.\"\n31\t      - R2.3:\n32\t          text: Must exit 1 when any named file does not exist or cannot be accessed, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n33\t\n34\t  R3:\n35\t    title: Format strings\n36\t    items:\n37\t      - R3.1:\n38\t          text: \"-c FORMAT or --format=FORMAT must use FORMAT as a printf-style format string. Must support directives: %a (access rights octal), %A (access rights human), %b (blocks allocated), %B (block size), %d (device number decimal), %D (device number hex), %f (raw mode hex), %F (file type), %g (group ID), %G (group name), %h (hard links), %i (inode), %m (mount point), %n (file name), %N (quoted file name with symlink target), %o (optimal I/O size), %s (total size bytes), %t (major device type hex), %T (minor device type hex), %u (user ID), %U (user name), %w (birth time human), %W (birth time epoch), %x (access time human), %X (access time epoch), %y (modify time human), %Y (modify time epoch), %z (change time human), %Z (change time epoch).\"\n39\t\n40\t  R4:\n41\t    title: Printf and terse output\n42\t    items:\n43\t      - R4.1:\n44\t          text: \"--printf=FORMAT must work like --format but interpret backslash escapes (\\\\n, \\\\t, etc.) and not append a trailing newline.\"\n45\t      - R4.2:\n46\t          text: \"-t or --terse must produce terse output (single line of space-separated fields) matching GNU stat --terse format.\"\n47\t\n48\t  R5:\n49\t    title: Filesystem status\n50\t    items:\n51\t      - R5.1:\n52\t          text: \"-f or --file-system must display filesystem status instead of file status. Output includes filesystem type, block size, total/free/available blocks and inodes.\"\n53\t\n54\t  R6:\n55\t    title: Filesystem format directives\n56\t    items:\n57\t      - R6.1:\n58\t          text: \"Format directives in --file-system mode differ from file mode: %a (free blocks available to non-root), %b (total blocks), %c (total inodes), %d (free inodes), %f (free blocks), %i (filesystem ID hex), %l (max filename length), %n (file name), %s (block size optimal), %S (fundamental block size), %t (filesystem type hex), %T (filesystem type name).\"\n59\t\n60\t  R7:\n61\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n62\t    items:\n63\t      - R7.1:\n64\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully.\n65\t      - R7.2:\n66\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or an invalid format directive is used.\n67\t      - R7.3:\n68\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n69\t\n70\tnon_goals:\n71\t  - cmd/stat does not implement SELinux context display (--context).\n72\t\n73\tacceptance_criteria:\n74\t  - id: AC1\n75\t    criterion: \"stat on a regular file produces multi-line status output matching gstat.\"\n76\t    traces:\n77\t      - R1.1\n78\t      - R2.1\n79\t      - R2.3\n80\t  - id: AC2\n81\t    criterion: \"stat -c '%s %n' file produces size and name, matching gstat -c '%s %n'.\"\n82\t    traces:\n83\t      - R3.1\n84\t  - id: AC3\n85\t    criterion: \"stat -f / produces filesystem status matching gstat -f /.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R5.1\n88\t      - R6.1\n89\t  - id: AC4\n90\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gstat passes for all required test cases.\"\n91\t    traces:\n92\t      - R1.1\n93\t      - R3.1\n94\t      - R5.1\n95\t  - id: AC5\n96\t    criterion: \"cmd/stat compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n97\t    traces:\n98\t      - R1.1\n99\t      - R2.1\n100\t      - R2.2\n101\t      - R2.3\n102\t      - R3.1\n103\t      - R4.1\n104\t      - R4.2\n105\t      - R5.1\n106\t      - R6.1\n107\t      - R7.1\n108\t      - R7.2\n109\t      - R7.3\n110\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01TCzA95i5oDnyyZ1LbTbAei","session_id":"8bcba697-70f2-4b61-a9af-34eaf485d661","uuid":"d5e7b64f-ce1a-4215-ae37-fa558bea7942","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:58:30.351Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RdZKowvjAq3qL4Jn3CMPSS","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t//go:build darwin\n5\t\n6\tpackage sys\n7\t\n8\timport (\n9\t\t\"fmt\"\n10\t\t\"os\"\n11\t\t\"syscall\"\n12\t\t\"time\"\n13\t)\n14\t\n15\t// fileInfoFromOS extracts FileInfo from os.FileInfo using the underlying\n16\t// Darwin-specific syscall.Stat_t.\n17\t// R1.4/R2.3: handles st_mtimespec/st_atimespec/st_ctimespec naming on Darwin.\n18\tfunc fileInfoFromOS(info os.FileInfo) (*FileInfo, error) {\n19\t\tstat, ok := info.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t)\n20\t\tif !ok {\n21\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"sys: underlying Sys() is not *syscall.Stat_t\")\n22\t\t}\n23\t\treturn &FileInfo{\n24\t\t\tMode:       info.Mode(),\n25\t\t\tSize:       stat.Size,\n26\t\t\tNlink:      uint64(stat.Nlink),\n27\t\t\tUid:        stat.Uid,\n28\t\t\tGid:        stat.Gid,\n29\t\t\tRdev:       uint64(stat.Rdev),\n30\t\t\tDev:        uint64(stat.Dev),\n31\t\t\tIno:        stat.Ino,\n32\t\t\tBlocks:     stat.Blocks,\n33\t\t\tBlksize:    int64(stat.Blksize),\n34\t\t\tModTime:    timespecToTime(stat.Mtimespec),\n35\t\t\tAccessTime: timespecToTime(stat.Atimespec),\n36\t\t\tChangeTime: timespecToTime(stat.Ctimespec),\n37\t\t\tInfo:       info,\n38\t\t}, nil\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\tfunc timespecToTime(ts syscall.Timespec) time.Time {\n42\t\treturn time.Unix(ts.Sec, ts.Nsec)\n43\t}\n44\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bcba697-70f2-4b61-a9af-34eaf485d661","uuid":"08df4256-8449-4919-b33f-9388ad59a027","timestamp":"2026-05-23T12:58:30.330Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5532/pkg/sys/stat_darwin.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n//go:build darwin\n\npackage sys\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"syscall\"\n\t\"time\"\n)\n\n// fileInfoFromOS extracts FileInfo from os.FileInfo using the underlying\n// Darwin-specific syscall.Stat_t.\n// R1.4/R2.3: handles st_mtimespec/st_atimespec/st_ctimespec naming on Darwin.\nfunc fileInfoFromOS(info os.FileInfo) (*FileInfo, error) {\n\tstat, ok := info.Sys().(*syscall.Stat_t)\n\tif !ok {\n\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"sys: underlying Sys() is not *syscall.Stat_t\")\n\t}\n\treturn &FileInfo{\n\t\tMode:       info.Mode(),\n\t\tSize:       stat.Size,\n\t\tNlink:      uint64(stat.Nlink),\n\t\tUid:        stat.Uid,\n\t\tGid:        stat.Gid,\n\t\tRdev:       uint64(stat.Rdev),\n\t\tDev:        uint64(stat.Dev),\n\t\tIno:        stat.Ino,\n\t\tBlocks:     stat.Blocks,\n\t\tBlksize:    int64(stat.Blksize),\n\t\tModTime:    timespecToTime(stat.Mtimespec),\n\t\tAccessTime: timespecToTime(stat.Atimespec),\n\t\tChangeTime: timespecToTime(stat.Ctimespec),\n\t\tInfo:       info,\n\t}, nil\n}\n\nfunc timespecToTime(ts syscall.Timespec) time.Time {\n\treturn time.Unix(ts.Sec, ts.Nsec)\n}\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
