{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AEgYCPeyCQLypL1HPdFgC2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see two differences:\n\n1. **File line quoting**: My output: `  File: '/tmp' -> 'private/tmp'`, GNU stat: `  File: /tmp -> private/tmp`\n   - GNU stat doesn't quote the filename in the default output on the File: line! But it does quote in %N.\n   \nWait, no. Looking more carefully at GNU stat, the File line doesn't use quotes in the default format. But my `writeFileLine` function calls `quoteFile(path)` which wraps in single quotes.\n\nActually, I need to look at this more carefully. In the GNU stat default format, the `%N` directive (which is what the File line uses) behaves differently. \n\nWhen outputting to a terminal, GNU stat uses `\\` quoting. When output is not a terminal, it uses different behavior. Looking at the actual outputs, GNU stat doesn't quote the filename in the default `File:` line, but it does show the quoted form in format string mode with `%N`. I need to fix the default format to not quote.\n\n2. **Device line format**: My output: `Device: 100000dh/16777229d`, GNU stat: `Device: 1,13`\n   - GNU stat on macOS shows the device as major,minor format instead of the hex representation I'm currently using.\n\nI'm realizing I confused two different things: the device that contains the file (shown as major,minor on the Device: line) versus the device type of character/block special files (shown as \"Device type: major,minor\"). On both Linux and macOS, the Device line uses major,minor format for the file's containing device, but I'm seeing inconsistencies in how GNU stat displays this across different systems that I need to investigate more carefully. So the device number is being displayed as major,minor format — that's 1 for the major device number and 13 for the minor. This suggests GNU coreutils might've changed how it formats device output in newer versions, moving away from the hexadecimal/decimal format to this major,minor representation. I should also check if the File line stops quoting filenames in the default format, and verify what version of gstat is being used to confirm these formatting changes.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":670,"cache_read_input_tokens":63977,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":670},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8bcba697-70f2-4b61-a9af-34eaf485d661","uuid":"ae13d6e0-363e-4957-9eb4-5db5ed115359"}
